#: intro/README.md:block 1 (header)
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "引言"

#: intro/README.md:block 2 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"The Internet and the World Wide Web have become more and more important for "
"people around the world as a source of all kinds of information, and a way "
"to exercise fundamental rights. At the same time, recent years have seen an "
"increase in all kinds of network censorship and other types of network "
"interference (see the reports from [OONI](https://ooni.org/reports/ \"Open "
"Observatory of Network Interference – Research reports\"), [Magma](https://"
"magma.lavafeld.org/publications/ \"Magma publications\"), [Censored Planet]"
"(https://censoredplanet.org/reports \"Censored Planet – Reports\")), both "
"from private and state actors."
msgstr ""
"互联网和万维网作为各类信息的来源以及行使基本权利的途径，对全球民众而言变得越"
"来越重要。与此同时，来自私人和国家行为的各种网络审查及其他类型的网络干扰（"
"参见 [OONI](https://ooni.org/reports/ "
"\"Open Observatory of Network Interference – Research reports\")、[Magma]"
"(https://magma.lavafeld.org/publications/ \"Magma publications\")、"
"[Censored Planet](https://censoredplanet.org/reports "
"\"Censored Planet – Reports\") 的报告）有所增加。"

#: intro/README.md:block 3 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"The Web relies on your devices being able to reach special computers called "
"*web servers* (run by content creators, publishers or Internet services "
"providers) that hold the content you want to retrieve, and to do so in a "
"synchronized way - more like having a live chat on the telephone than "
"exchanging some letters. Unfortunately, this requires that the web server "
"you need is connected to the network and has enough available resources to "
"talk to your device at that moment."
msgstr ""
"万维网的运行依赖于您的设备能够连接到被称为*网络服务器*的特殊计算机（由内容创"
"作者、发布者或互联网服务提供商运营），这些计算机存储着您想要获取的内容，并且"
"这种连接需要以同步方式进行：这更像是打电话进行实时聊天，而非互通书信。不幸的"
"是是，这要求您所需的网络服务器必须接入网络，且在此时有足够的可用资源与您的设"
"备进行通信。"

#: intro/README.md:block 4 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"The advent of *content delivery networks* (or CDNs, like the commercial "
"Akamai and Cloudflare, or the civil society-oriented Deflect) has taken some "
"of the load off these web servers by distributing copies of the content to "
"data centers all over the world, so that it can be closer to your devices "
"and thus faster to reach, while keeping the origin servers protected from "
"direct access. However, currently CDN servers (and thus the organizations "
"that run them) need to be trusted by both the origin server and your "
"devices, and they also need to be reachable at all times."
msgstr ""
"*内容分发网络*（即 CDN，例如商业性质的 Akamai 和 Cloudflare ，"
"或是面向公民社会的 "
"Deflect）的出现，通过将内容副本分发到全球各地的数据中心，使其更靠近您的设备，"
"从而更快地访问，减轻了这些网络服务器的部分负担。 "
"同时还能保护源服务器免受直接访问。然而，目前的 CDN "
"服务器（以及运营它们的组织）需要同时获得源服务器和您的设备的信任，而且它们还"
"需要始终保持可访问状态。"

#: intro/README.md:block 5 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"Unfortunately again, there are situations in which general connectivity is "
"scarce (developing countries or underserved, impoverished or rural regions), "
"expensive (with some countries charging more for international traffic) or "
"has been actively blocked by an state player (explicitly or as a result of a "
"general shutdown). In these cases, reaching origin web servers or even CDN "
"servers is difficult or impossible, and your device will not be able to get "
"that content - even if I was somehow able to access it a few hours ago and "
"we're living some streets apart."
msgstr ""
"不幸的是，在一些情况下，整体网络连接会出现匮乏（如发展中国家或服务不足、贫困"
"地区及农村地区）、成本高昂（部分国家对国际流量收取更多费用），或是被国家主动"
"封锁（可能是明确封锁，也可能因全面断网导致）。在这些情况下，"
"访问源网络服务器乃至 CDN "
"服务器会变得困难甚至无法实现，您的设备也就无法获取相关内容，即便几小时前我刚"
"设法访问过这些内容。"

#: intro/README.md:block 6 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"This is where Ceno Browser and Ouinet come into play. This chapter will "
"introduce you to them."
msgstr "这就是CENO浏览器和Ouinet发挥作用的地方。本章将向你进行介绍。"

